  "id": "COMPOUND:43644 - PROTEIN:4961",
  "verbalization": "Blepharocalyxin D is implicated in the interaction with FaDu through multiple pathways, all involving the Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9. This enzyme is a target of two distinct compounds, 6-Hydroxy-2-[2-(2-hydroxyphenyl) ethyl]chromone and 5-[(2S,3R)-3-(hydroxymethyl)-7-[(E)-3-hydroxyprop-1-enyl]-5-methoxy-2,3-dihydro-1,4-benzodioxin-2-yl]-3-methoxybenzene-1,2-diol, which both direct their targets to FaDu. The consistent presence of these intermediates in the pathway suggests a potential mechanism by which Blepharocalyxin D may exert its effects on FaDu, possibly through the modulation of the SDR family member 9, which in turn influences the activity of FaDu. The evidence is supported by multiple high-scoring pathways, indicating a plausible and well-documented interaction. The mechanism appears to involve the SDR family member 9 as a key mediator, with the compounds acting as activators or modulators of this enzyme, ultimately leading to a target effect on FaDu. The evidence is robust and consistent, but the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
